 "final_text_tail": "I haven't confirmed the failing call. `normalize_image` and `_get_image_id_bytes` already suppress EXIF exceptions. That leaves `load_bytes`, which only converts `OSError`, `UnidentifiedImageError` and `SyntaxError`. A malformed EXIF block that raises some other exception during `image.load()` or the mode conversion would escape it and become a 500.\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"vllm/multimodal/media/image.py\", \"vllm/multimodal/image.py\", \"vllm/multimodal/hasher.py\"], \"functions\": [\"ImageMediaIO.load_bytes\", \"normalize_image\", \"_get_image_id_bytes\", \"MultiModalHasher.serialize_item\", \"open_image\"]}\n```",
